      "title": "The Ontological Definition of Databricks Genie Ontology via OntoRank",
      "url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=voZXeHP2qWQ",
      "published_at": "2026-09-21T10:00:36+00:00",
      "author": "Advancing Analytics",
      "summary": "One of the biggest announcements at Data + AI Summit 2026 was the preview of Genie Ontology. Essentially giving Genie One a turbo boost to allow it to infer context, glorious context, from any snippet of information it can get it's hands on.\n\nThis is a hugely powerful, industry changing tool... and yet I spent a lot of the day correcting people that it's not, actually, an ontology. But why does that matter? What does that mean? And what, if not an ontology, actually is it?\n\nIn this video Simon dives into the Genie Ontology release, OntoRank, the algorithm behind it, and the change that this new product is going to bring to your organisations and the tired idea of Ontologies themselves!",
